<title>USA: Fannie Mae to redeem $1175 mln in issues.</title>
<headline>Fannie Mae to redeem $1175 mln in issues.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Fannie Mae on Thursday said it will redeem all outstanding amounts of one debenture issue totaling $650 million, one global issue totaling $300 million and three medium-term note issues totaling $225 million.</p>
<p>The debenture has series number SM-2004-G. Its terms are</p>
<p>as follows.</p>
<p>  Principal     Interest    Maturity    Cusip     Redemption</p>
<p>   Amount	   Rate	  Date	Number	Date</p>
<p> $650 million     8.05	07/14/04   31359CAU9   07/14/97</p>
<p>The terms of the medium-term notes are as follows.</p>
<p>  Principal     Interest    Maturity    Cusip     Redemption</p>
<p>   Amount	   Rate	  Date	Number	Date</p>
<p> $100 million     7.15	06/26/01   31364CFB9   06/26/97</p>
<p>  $75 million     7.37	06/26/01   31364CFD5   06/26/97</p>
<p>  $50 million     7.625*    09/21/06   31364A3E0   07/14/97</p>
<p>*current interest rate</p>
<p>The terms of the global issue are as follows.</p>
<p>  Principal     Interest    Maturity    Cusip     Redemption</p>
<p>   Amount	   Rate	  Date	Number	Date</p>
<p> $300 million     7.00	06/25/99   31359MAK9   06/25/97</p>
<p>The redemption price of the issues will be 100 percent of the principal amount plus interest accrued to the redemption date, Fannie Mae said.</p>
</text>
